## 15\. Secria VPN-Specific Terms

In addition to the general Terms above, the following terms apply to your use of Secria VPN.

### Service Availability

Secria VPN is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis. Features may change, break, or be removed without notice; service availability, speed, and reliability are not guaranteed; and connectivity issues may occur. You agree not to rely on the Service for critical or life-safety purposes.

### Acceptable Use

You agree not to use Secria VPN to:

* Engage in illegal activity under applicable law.  
* Send spam or malware, or conduct phishing attacks.  
* Attack, scan, or probe other networks or systems.  
* Infringe on intellectual property rights.  
* Distribute child sexual abuse material.  
* Conduct denial-of-service attacks.

Violation may result in immediate account termination without notice.

### No-Log Policy

We do not log your browsing activity, DNS queries, traffic contents, or the source IP addresses you connect from. To operate the Service and protect your account, we retain limited connection metadata — the device and Secria account associated with a session, the VPN server used, the VPN-assigned internal IP address, and connection timestamps (such as when a device last connected). We never record the websites you visit or the contents of your traffic. See our [Privacy Policy](https://secria.me/privacy-policy) for full details.

### Account & Devices

Your Secria VPN access is linked to your Secria account and is subject to the device limit shown in the app. You are responsible for maintaining the security of your credentials.

